# Open Knowledge Format

OKF is a **file format**, not a product. A bundle is a directory of Markdown
records with YAML frontmatter, typed collections, and links. The files stay
diffable in git. Nothing in the record body is executed.

That is distinct from a hosted wiki, a proprietary catalog schema, or Google
Cloud Knowledge Catalog. OKF is the shared contract; tools implement it.

## Three names

| Name | Job |
| --- | --- |
| **OKF** | The format: inert Markdown, YAML, collections, graph of concept links. |
| **`okf` crate** | Portable Rust engine in this repo: parse, validate, graph, search, artifacts. No HTML or desktop. |
| **`okmate`** | The application: CLI, Askama preview, optional macOS window. Depends on `okf` only. |

A **bundle** is one root directory of OKF files (for example this repo’s
`knowledge/`). `okmate check` / `inspect` / `search` / `build` take one root.

## Specification and references

- [open-knowledge-format](https://github.com/GoogleCloudPlatform/open-knowledge-format)
  — canonical specification repository
- [SPEC.md](https://github.com/GoogleCloudPlatform/open-knowledge-format/blob/main/SPEC.md)
  — format text
- [How OKF can improve data sharing](https://cloud.google.com/blog/products/data-analytics/how-the-open-knowledge-format-can-improve-data-sharing)
  — short public overview
- [`okf/README.md`](https://github.com/koliyo/okmate/blob/main/okf/README.md)
  — engine this repository ships (profiles, graph, artifacts)

## Profiles

`Profile::Base` is portable OKF. `Profile::Strict` adds owners and evidence.
This repository’s knowledge tree uses `--profile strict`.

## Artifacts

`okmate build` writes `catalog.json`, `search.json`, `validation.json`, a
bundle `llms.txt`, and Askama HTML for **one** bundle. That bundle `llms.txt`
is not this site’s `/llms.txt`. The product-site file is authored for visiting
agents (`site/llms.txt`).

## What okmate does not do

`okmate` does not compile Rocdown. `rocdown` refuses OKF records and points
here. Keep project knowledge in `knowledge/` and product pages in `site/`.
